"""flowd: dictation for the whole desktop (Flow).

Hold the key (the shell's `flowHold` shortcut), speak, release: the audio streams to Gemini 3.5
Transcribe Live while you speak (fillers and self-corrections removed, lists formatted, your word
list as its vocabulary), the text is final a few hundred ms after the key goes up, and it is typed
where your cursor is. If the stream fails, Gemini 2.5 Flash hears the recording instead.

Socket $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flow.sock, JSON lines:
  -> {"op":"start"} {"op":"stop"} {"op":"cancel"} {"op":"status"} {"op":"watch"}
     {"op":"file","path":WAV,"dry":true}   feed a 16 kHz mono WAV instead of the mic (checks)
     {"op":"insert","text":..}   type a past dictation where the cursor is (the palette's history)
  <- {"ev":"state","state":"idle|listening|writing|error","text":..}  (+ build/proto on watch)
     {"ev":"level","v":0..1}   {"ev":"done","text":..,"raw":..,"ms":{..}}
Files: ~/.config/flow/config.json, ~/.config/flow/words.txt (one term per line),
       ~/.local/state/flow/history.jsonl (the last 300 dictations, local only).
Google login: the gcloud user token, renewed in the background (no key files on disk).
"""
